>$a$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\"><b>B</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$b$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\"><b>C</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$c$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our diagram.\n\n- There is $1$ arrow starting at Station A and ending at Station B. So, there is only one route from $A$ to $B,$ and so $a=1.$\n\n- There is $1$ arrow starting at Station B and ending at Station B. So, there is only one route from $B$ to $B,$ and so $b=1.$\n\n- There are no arrows starting at Station C and ending at Station A. So, there are no routes from $C$ to $A,$ and so $c=0.$\n\nAs a result, our route matrix is the following:\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\">To:</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\"><b>A</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\"><b>B</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\"><b>C</b></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" rowspan=\"3\">From:</td>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\"><b>A</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\"><b>B</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" width=\"30\"><b>C</b></td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\na+b+c=1+1+0=2.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186271965 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "53144731-7725-5907-918b-d5713b670e0d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270007} {:answer/id #uuid "5a44cfba-69bd-514f-beb9-1f9c988affe3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270072} {:answer/id #uuid "60c809fd-5f78-5ac9-aa54-4cdd1b54286e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270124} {:answer/id #uuid "70398bab-0b9a-5aa7-adad-d0d070ded60a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270262} {:answer/id #uuid "e913dca1-03c6-5d39-8cb8-3922ed7d4b59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271307}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e913dca1-03c6-5d39-8cb8-3922ed7d4b59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271307} :answer-field/id #uuid "35c51080-e239-5221-93b7-5dbdc5f93e34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271614}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6e096d82-d20e-57bf-96a5-ec2c24ce0473" :question/math-academy-id "q-139719" :question/problem "![](images/0e/0ed581569bdc7c4f269f4cdf48d3ae20205627312641ff5b06daa2dca5a0e168.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows bus routes between four stations, where nodes represent the stations and arrows represent the directed routes between them. The (incomplete) route matrix below represents information about the number of routes between each of the four stations. Find the value of $a+b+c.$\n\n|  |  | To: |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **A** | **B** | **C** | **D** |\n| From: | **A** | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $a$ |\n| **B** | $0$ | $0$ | $b$ | $0$ |  |\n| **C** | $0$ | $0$ | $c$ | $1$ |  |\n| **D** | $0$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "Let's examine our diagram.\n\n- There are $2$ arrows starting at Station A and ending at Station D. So, there are two routes from $A$ to $D,$ and so $a=2.$\n\n- There is $1$ arrow starting at Station B and ending at Station C. So, there is only one route from $B$ to $C,$ and so $b=1.$\n\n- There are no arrows starting at Station C and ending at Station C. So, there are no routes from $C$ to $C,$ and so $c=0.$\n\nAs a result, our route matrix is the following:\n\n|  |  | To: |  |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **A** | **B** | **C** | **D** |\n| From: | **A** | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ | $2$ |\n| **B** | $0$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ |  |\n| **C** | $0$ | $0$ | $0$ | $1$ |  |\n| **D** | $0$ | $0$ | $1$ | $0$ |  |\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\na+b+c=2+1+0=3.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299744 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ffc48ff-1011-56e8-978d-23ac82a79306" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297690}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ffc48ff-1011-56e8-978d-23ac82a79306" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186297690} :answer-field/id #uuid "28ebc2c3-8f30-59dc-a757-e2f3006a8b32" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298775} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ab4fcc6-76c4-5164-a6f8-e99687699fd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298155}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ab4fcc6-76c4-5164-a6f8-e99687699fd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186298155} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e857817-9ed7-5435-956e-848cd74bf5b0" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186299159} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dfcfbf74-a02e-5cd5-884b-9d1f0073aa1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 1